{
  "about": "Requests that pin the parcel API's contract for the GeoDjango port (DIC-2147). Each entry is replayed as-is. Fields: name (unique), method, path (with query string), body (JSON, optional), raw_body (text sent as-is, for malformed bodies) and content_type (optional), auth ('admin' sends X-Admin-Token from PV_ADMIN_TOKEN for FastAPI and/or 'Authorization: Token' from PV_STAFF_TOKEN for the Django port, which retired the shared key in DIC-2151; skipped when neither is set), headers (optional; <<repeat:CHAR:N>> expands to N copies of CHAR, in paths and body strings), known_issue (a ticket id: the route is broken today, so its response is reported but not recorded or failed on), compare ('full' = status, contract headers and body; 'shape' = status, contract headers, list lengths and structure but not values, for results cut off at their limit: /parcels and /cohort have no ORDER BY, so which rows come back is arbitrary; 'status' = status and content type only, for routes whose body comes from a third party, and for the admin refusals, whose wording differs by design since the Django port retired the shared key (DIC-2151, ADR 0013)). Unordered lists of objects with an id are compared by id, so a different order is only a warning. Never add a request that sends email, writes config or reports a fake client error: those routes are only exercised with requests they reject.",
